  "level": "B1",
  "title": "The present subjunctive",
  "tagline": "Quiero que vengas, ojalá llueva: wishes, requests and feelings about others.",
  "goal": "Form the present subjunctive, including irregular verbs, and use it after wishes, requests, emotions and ojalá.",
  "minutes": 12,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "formas",
      "title": "How to form it",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Take the **yo** form of the present, drop the -o, and switch the vowel: -ar verbs take **e**, -er / -ir verbs take **a**. Irregular yo forms carry over: *tengo → tenga*."
        },
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "persons": ["yo", "tú", "él / ella / usted", "nosotros", "ellos / ellas / ustedes"],
          "verbs": [
            { "verb": "hablar", "meaning": "to speak", "forms": ["habl{e}", "habl{es}", "habl{e}", "habl{emos}", "habl{en}"] },
            { "verb": "comer", "meaning": "to eat", "forms": ["com{a}", "com{as}", "com{a}", "com{amos}", "com{an}"] },
            { "verb": "tener", "meaning": "to have (tengo)", "forms": ["teng{a}", "teng{as}", "teng{a}", "teng{amos}", "teng{an}"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Irregular", "Subjunctive"],
          "rows": [
            ["*ser*", "*sea, seas, sea, seamos, sean*"],
            ["*ir*", "*vaya, vayas, vaya, vayamos, vayan*"],
            ["*estar*", "*esté, estés, esté, estemos, estén*"],
            ["*saber*", "*sepa, sepas…*"],
            ["*haber*", "*haya, hayas…*"],
            ["*dar*", "*dé, des, dé, demos, den*"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "deseos",
      "title": "Wishes and requests about others",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When one person wants, asks or recommends that **someone else** does something, the second verb goes in the subjunctive. English often uses an infinitive here: «I want **you to come**» = *Quiero que **vengas***."
        },
        {
          "type": "formula",
          "text": "querer / pedir / recomendar / necesitar + que + subjuntivo"
        },
        {
          "type": "examples",
          "items": [
            { "fr": "Quiero que {vengas} a mi fiesta.", "tr": "I want you to come to my party." },
            { "fr": "Te pido que me {ayudes}.", "tr": "I'm asking you to help me." },
            { "fr": "El médico recomienda que {descanse}.", "tr": "The doctor recommends that I rest." }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "Same person → infinitive",
          "text": "*Quiero ir* (I want to go) but *Quiero que {vayas}* (I want you to go). The subjunctive needs two different people."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "emociones",
      "title": "Feelings, judgments and ojalá",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Trigger", "Example", "English"],
          "rows": [
            ["*Me alegra que…*", "*Me alegra que {estés} aquí.*", "I'm glad you're here."],
            ["*Siento que…*", "*Siento que no {puedas} venir.*", "I'm sorry you can't come."],
            ["*Es importante que…*", "*Es importante que {lleguemos} a tiempo.*", "It's important that we arrive on time."],
            ["*Es mejor que…*", "*Es mejor que {vayas} al médico.*", "You'd better go to the doctor."],
            ["*Ojalá (que)…*", "*Ojalá {haga} sol mañana.*", "I hope it's sunny tomorrow."]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
